        "workflow": {
          "name": "archon-attention",
          "description": "The attention pause every public SDLC stage shares; a building block, not a\nworkflow to run. After a pass of the stage, one agent decides whether its ending\nhas a next step. When it has none, the run pauses as one select attention item: what\nended and why it matters, the agent's recommendation with its confidence and\nevidence, the declared choices (`rerun` the stage, take its pull request out of\ndraft with `ready`, or `finish` with the outcome as it stands), what waiting costs,\nand the links. The next pass acts on the answer.\n\nA public stage (archon-deliver, archon-plan, archon-triage, archon-review,\narchon-ship) runs its `-block` and this block, include id `attend`, as the body of\none loop: a gate node that runs the stage on the first pass and after a `rerun`\nanswer, read as `$LOOP_PREV.attend__ask.output.decision`; the stage, whose work\ngets `$LOOP_PREV.attend__settle.output.brief` and the answer's text appended; and\nthis block with `trigger_rule: all_done`, so it settles a pass whose stage was\nskipped. A pass whose stage failed asks nothing, and the stage's failure fails the\nrun. The loop ends on `$attend.output.done`, and `$attend.output.outcome` is the\nstage's outcome. A workflow that composes a stage includes the `-block` instead and\nowns what follows its ending, so it never raises a second item.\n",
          "nodes": [
            {
              "id": "answer",
              "kind": "exec",
              "script": "answer",
              "runtime": "bun",
              "with": {
                "outcome": "$INPUTS.outcome",
